;******** Final instructions to convert to bufr (on Jul 08th 2026) **************************
cd  /discover/nobackup/mganesha/DSI_PBL/fromWei
1. Edit run_bufr2ioda_gnssro.j to run the bufr to netcdf converter program on "bending angle/meta data" and "refractivity" files separately.
;Uncomment line 37 for meta data/bending angle
srun -n 1 $bufrbuild/build/bin/bufr2netcdf.x  ./input/gdas1.240716.t12z.gpsro.tm00.bufr_d gnssro_metadata_bending_angle_nosplits.yaml ./output/gnssro_metadata_bending_angle_2024071612.nc4
;Uncomment line 36 for refractivity
srun -n 1 $bufrbuild/build/bin/bufr2netcdf.x  ./input/gdas1.240716.t12z.gpsro.tm00.bufr_d gnssro.yaml ./output/gnssro_obs_2024071612.nc4

2. gnssro.yaml file is the same as "gnssro_nosplits_refractivity_only_metadata_safe_annotated.yaml"

;*********** Final script to produce GNSS RO PBLH files for assimilation WITH consideration of surface elevation data ********
1. Go to scripts folder ( /discover/nobackup/mganesha/DSI_PBL/fromWei/scripts) and edit "read_gnssro_twopeaks_wsurfelev_qc_compact.ncl" for date and time under "User settings". This script is based on "read_gnssro_twopeaks_clean4.ncl" except that it considers GEOS-FP (or alternatively MERRA-2) surface elevation when calculating second peak. Save the output here: /discover/nobackup/mganesha/DSI_PBL/fromWei/scripts/output/twopeaks/thresh40_FPsfcelev_qc/ or alternatively /discover/nobackup/mganesha/DSI_PBL/fromWei/scripts/output/twopeaks/thresh40_sfcelev_qc/ for MERRA-2. 

2. Plot to check output:plot_ncfile_pblh_wsfcelev_qc.ncl

; Same script but python version with surface elevation data
3. For running python script:

module purge
module load python/GEOSpyD/26.3.2-0/3.14
rehash

;Verify packages:
python3 -c "import numpy, netCDF4; print('NumPy:', numpy.__version__); print('netCDF4:', netCDF4.__version__)"

;Run command:
python3 read_gnssro_twopeaks_wsurfelev_qc_compact.py --date 20240903 --hour 00

